  "d7: 🍽️ Somchai taps the pantry's fullest jar. \"More than we can eat before it turns. Rendering fat instead — the lamps won't fill themselves.\"",
  "d7: 🍽️ David taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d8: 🍽️ Somchai leaves the foraging basket at the door. \"The pantry can't take more — sitting with the elders instead.\"",
  "d8: 🍽️ Thabo leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d9: 🍽️ Somchai rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d9: 🍽️ Eric carries the day's surplus to the pantry door, thinks better of it, and turns back to the fire. \"It'll only rot in there. We eat.\"",
  "d10: 🍽️ Somchai eyes the groaning pantry shelves and packs light today. \"No point hauling what'll rot. Mending the nets instead.\"",
  "d10: 🍽️ Jorge looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d11: 🍽️ David weighs the day's basket against the pantry shelves and puts it down. \"Enough. Carving bowls instead — we're down to the cracked ones.\"",
  "d11: 🍽️ Thabo sets the sharing basket down by the fire instead of the pantry. \"Full shelves don't need my little more.\"",
  "d12: 🍽️ Eric counts the pantry jars twice, then sets down the gathering sack. \"We're eating well. Sharpening the skinning knives instead.\"",
  "d12: 🍽️ Katarina taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
